@host = http://localhost:5000
@api = {{host}}/api
@ticket = 1
@requester = 4
@agent = 6
@supervisor = 3

### Health check
GET {{host}}/

### List tickets
GET {{api}}/tickets

### Log in (password for every demo user is Test@1234)
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "supervisor@helpdesk.local",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### Create a ticket (requester id 4 = Demo Requester, category 1 = Network / IT)
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Internet not working in C Block",
  "description": "No connection since morning",
  "category_id": 1,
  "priority": "High",
  "requester_id": 4
}
### Create: IT ticket, High priority (goes to an IT agent, status Open)
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Internet not working in C Block",
  "description": "No connection since morning",
  "category_id": 1,
  "priority": "High",
  "requester_id": 4
}

### Create: Electrical ticket, priority from impact x urgency (High + High = Critical, 24x7 clock)
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Power cut in the lab",
  "description": "Whole lab has no power",
  "category_id": 2,
  "impact": "High",
  "urgency": "High",
  "requester_id": 4
}

### One ticket with its history (change the 1 to your ticket id)
GET {{api}}/tickets/1

### Filter: open tickets of IT agent one (user 6)
GET {{api}}/tickets?assignee_id=6&status=Open

### Search by number or subject
GET {{api}}/tickets?q=internet
### What can this user do next on the ticket? (change @agent to try other users)
GET {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/transitions
x-user-id: {{agent}}

### Agent starts work: Open -> In Progress (counts as the first response)
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{agent}}

{
  "status": "In Progress"
}

### Agent puts the ticket on hold (SLA clock stops)
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{agent}}

{
  "status": "On Hold",
  "reason": "Waiting for the requester's screenshot"
}

### Requester replies: On Hold -> In Progress (SLA clock starts again)
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{requester}}

{
  "status": "In Progress"
}

### Agent resolves the ticket
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{agent}}

{
  "status": "Resolved"
}

### Requester is not happy: reopen (allowed for 7 days)
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{requester}}

{
  "status": "Reopened"
}

### Requester confirms: close (only from Resolved)
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{requester}}

{
  "status": "Closed"
}

### Should FAIL with 403: the requester tries to resolve
PATCH {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{requester}}

{
  "status": "Resolved"
}

### Supervisor assigns / re-assigns the ticket to agent 7
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json
x-user-id: {{supervisor}}

{
  "assignee_id": 7
}

### Supervisor: auto-assign a ticket that has no agent yet
POST {{api}}/tickets/{{ticket}}/auto-assign
x-user-id: {{supervisor}}
### Categories, teams, statuses, priorities (for the dropdowns)
GET {{api}}/meta

### Agents with their open tickets (Supervisor / Admin)
GET {{api}}/meta/agents?team_id=1
x-user-id: {{supervisor}}

### My notifications (agent)
GET {{api}}/notifications
x-user-id: {{agent}}

### Notifications of agent 8 (the Electrical agent)
GET {{api}}/notifications
x-user-id: 8

### Notifications of the supervisor
GET {{api}}/notifications
x-user-id: {{supervisor}}

### Mark all my notifications as read
POST {{api}}/notifications/read-all
x-user-id: {{agent}}

### Create: Critical ticket (for the SLA job test below)
POST {{api}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "Server room is down",
  "description": "No power in the server room",
  "category_id": 2,
  "impact": "High",
  "urgency": "High",
  "requester_id": 4
}